      "text": "Below are strong CRM options for small consulting firms, emphasizing ease of use, relationship management, proposal follow-up, and project handoff.\n\n**Pricing is approximate U.S. list pricing per user/month with annual billing. Ratings are rounded Capterra user ratings and fluctuate over time.**\n\n| CRM | Capterra rating* | Starting price | Consulting-relevant features | Best for |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| **monday sales CRM** | **~4.7/5** | From **$12/user/mo**; usually 3-user minimum | Highly customizable pipelines, dashboards, email sync, workflow automation, account management, post-sale project boards | Firms wanting to manage sales and delivery in one flexible workspace |\n| **Capsule CRM** | **~4.5/5** | Free for limited use; paid from **~$18/user/mo** | Simple contact history, opportunities, tasks, email integration, project boards, Xero/QuickBooks integrations | Small firms prioritizing simplicity and fast adoption |\n| **Freshsales** | **~4.5/5** | Free limited plan; paid from **$9/user/mo** | Built-in email and phone, lead scoring, multiple pipelines, workflows, activity tracking, AI assistance | Value-conscious firms that want communications built in |\n| **Pipedrive** | **~4.5/5** | From **~$15/user/mo** | Excellent visual pipeline, activity reminders, email sync, automations, forecasting, proposal/document tools and project add-ons | Consultancies with a structured, deal-driven sales process |\n| **HubSpot CRM / Sales Hub** | **~4.5/5** | Free CRM; Starter **~$15\u201320/user/mo** | Forms, meeting scheduling, email tracking, pipelines, marketing automation, ticketing and extensive integrations | Firms wanting a free starting point and broad marketing/service ecosystem |\n| **Copper CRM** | **~4.4/5** | From **~$9/user/mo** | Deep Gmail, Calendar and Drive integration; relationship tracking, pipelines, workflow automation and project management | Google Workspace\u2013centric consulting firms |\n| **Zoho CRM** | **~4.3/5** | Free for up to 3 users; paid from **$14/user/mo** | Custom modules, workflow rules, lead scoring, forecasting, Blueprint process management, Zoho Books/Projects integration | Firms needing strong customization at a low price |\n| **Insightly CRM** | **~4.0/5** | From **$29/user/mo** | CRM-to-project conversion, relationship linking, task and milestone tracking, workflow automation, dashboards | Firms that need a clear handoff from winning work to delivering it |\n\n\\*Ratings should be treated as directional: review counts differ substantially, and scores change as new reviews are added.\n\n## Best choices by use case\n\n- **Best overall for a straightforward sales pipeline:** **Pipedrive**\n- **Best free starting option:** **HubSpot**\n- **Best value and customization:** **Zoho CRM**\n- **Best for Google Workspace:** **Copper**\n- **Best for integrated calling and email:** **Freshsales**\n- **Best for combining sales with project delivery:** **monday sales CRM**\n- **Best for very small firms wanting simplicity:** **Capsule**\n- **Best CRM-to-project handoff:** **Insightly**\n\n## Important cost considerations\n\nThe entry price can be misleading, so check whether your required plan includes:\n\n- Two-way email synchronization\n- Workflow automation\n- Multiple pipelines\n- Proposal or document generation\n- Reporting and forecasting\n- QuickBooks, Xero or accounting integrations\n- Project management\n- Minimum seat requirements\n- AI features, which may require higher tiers or usage credits\n\nFor most small consulting firms, I would shortlist **Pipedrive, HubSpot, Zoho and monday sales CRM**. Choose **Pipedrive** for sales discipline, **HubSpot** for marketing and growth, **Zoho** for value, or **monday** if project delivery is nearly as important as lead management.\n\nIf the firm also needs **time tracking, utilization, resource planning and client billing**, a professional-services platform such as **Productive, Scoro, Accelo or Kantata** may fit better than a standalone CRM."
